  <issue>
  handle spline interpolation methods in `interpn`
As long as `interpn` is (mostly) a convenience wrapper over RegularGridInterpolator, it may make sense for it to grow support for new `cubic`, `quintic` and `pchip` modes which were added for 1.9.0.

Currently it only supports `nearest` and `linear` modes of RGI, plus `splinef2d` which should probably kept for backwards compatibility.
